  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile RNA modeling with scvi_n200 improves validation accuracy from 0.520 single-profile to about 0.650 multiprofile, with avgpool and transformer aggregation nearly tied. The key uncertainty is whether this multiprofile gain is a general property of the profile setting or specific to the scvi representation. Testing pca_n2000 with multiprofile and simple avgpool directly compares against the single-profile pca baseline and the scvi multiprofile results, helping isolate the effect of profile setting before adding image or fusion complexity. This is a lower-complexity, high-information experiment under a limited budget."
}

